# The appliance's one privileged escape hatch. tribd runs as a systemd
# USER unit under a nologin service account with no capabilities, and
# partitioning a drive needs CAP_SYS_ADMIN.
#
# No argument restriction, deliberately: sudoers wildcard matching is
# famously escapable, so validation belongs in the script — which is
# root-owned and not writable by the caller. The grant is therefore "may
# run this exact program as root", nothing narrower and nothing wider, and
# the program is the thing to review.
#
# Consequence, stated so nobody has to discover it: anyone who can reach
# the console can erase an attached USB drive. That is the feature.
tributary ALL=(root:root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/lib/tributary/format-drive.sh
